---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import FormattedDate from '../components/FormattedDate.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import authorPhoto from '../assets/denis-ethier.png';

const posts = (await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => {
	return import.meta.env.DEV || !data.draft;
})).sort(
	(a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf()
);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<!-- Top Medical Disclaimer Bar -->
		<div class="top-disclaimer-bar">
			<strong>Medical Disclaimer:</strong> I am sharing my personal lived experiences, self-experiments, and what worked for my own body. I am a patient, not a doctor. Always consult your physician or specialist before trying any new health&nbsp;protocol.
		</div>

		<Header />
		<main>
			<!-- Hero Section (Centered) -->
			<section class="hero-centered-wrapper">
				<div class="hero-centered-header">
					<h1 class="hero-centered-title">How I stopped my BMS</h1>
					<p class="hero-centered-subtitle">When my mouth started burning, doctors told me everything looked completely normal. I refused to accept that. I treated my body like a system, tracked every variable, and found the protocol that brought me lasting&nbsp;relief.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="hero-video-centered">
					<div class="video-responsive-wrapper">
						<iframe 
							src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/BM8qUgA8yPE?rel=0" 
							title="How I stopped my BMS"
							allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" 
							allowfullscreen
						></iframe>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Personal Story Section (For Reading Without Watching Video) -->
				<article class="personal-story-section">
					<div class="nutshell-box">
						<h3>In a Nutshell</h3>
						<p>I woke up one morning in 2025 with severe oral burning that reached an 8/10 every afternoon. After months of normal tests, negative swabs, and doctors telling me everything looked fine, I took an engineering and system-design approach. By eliminating nocturnal mouth-drying through gentle mouth taping, cutting dietary acids and seed oils via a strict carnivore protocol, and restoring mucosal electrolytes, my pain dropped by 80% in one week and reached full remission in 30&nbsp;days.</p>
					</div>

					<div class="story-body">
						<h2>The Mysterious Burn and the Medical Runaround</h2>
						<p>It started without warning: a scalded feeling along the sides and tip of my tongue, exactly like drinking boiling tea. Within weeks, the sensation became a constant background roar. By 3:00 PM every day, talking felt like running coarse sandpaper across raw tissue.</p>
						<p>I did what every rational person does: I booked appointments with dentists, doctors, and ENT specialists. They inspected my tongue, ran comprehensive autoimmune panels, checked my vitamin B12, ferritin, and thyroid levels. Every single test came back completely normal. Being told you are completely healthy while your mouth feels like it is on fire is an isolating, surreal experience.</p>

						<h2>Treating the Body as an Engineering System</h2>
						<p>Having spent over 15 years in product design and technology systems, I know one fundamental truth: unexplained errors always have root causes. If the system is failing, you simply have not isolated the right variables or inspected the correct telemetry yet.</p>
						<p>I stopped relying on vague reassurances and built a comprehensive personal tracking matrix:</p>
						<ul>
							<li><strong>Mucosal Hydration:</strong> Nighttime mouth breathing and evaporative drying stripping the protective oral mucin barrier.</li>
							<li><strong>Biochemical Acidity:</strong> Hidden acids, food preservatives, and sugars fueling systemic neuro-inflammation.</li>
							<li><strong>Nerve Desensitization:</strong> Restoring cellular lipids and bioavailable B-vitamins to calm hyperactive lingual nerves.</li>
						</ul>

						<h2>The Protocol That Ended My Burn</h2>
						<p>The turning point was addressing my nighttime oral dryness. I began gentle nighttime mouth taping to ensure 100% nasal breathing while asleep. Waking up with a naturally moist mouth instead of parched tissue immediately dropped the morning baseline burn.</p>
						<p>Pairing this with an elimination carnivore diet removed all fermentable sugars and plant acids, starving oral inflammation. Within 14 days, the burning dropped from an agonizing 8/10 down to a mild 1/10. Today, my BMS is in sustained remission.</p>

						<div class="story-author-tag">
							<Image src={authorPhoto} alt="Denis Ethier" class="story-author-avatar" width={108} height={108} />
							<div class="story-author-info">
								<h4>Denis Ethier</h4>
								<p>Software designer, builder & founder of Decoding The Burn</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- Email Capture CTA -->
				<div class="hero-cta-capture">
					<div class="cta-capture-box">
						<h2>Stay Updated on my progress</h2>
						<p>I document every self-experiment I conduct, new research papers I dissect, and the daily habits that keep my BMS in remission. Drop your email to follow&nbsp;along.</p>
						
						<!-- MailerLite Form Embed -->
						<div class="ml-embedded" data-form="0R4iAA"></div>

						<!-- Quick Email Capture Form -->
						<form class="email-capture-form" action="/join" method="get">
							<input 
								type="email" 
								name="email" 
								placeholder="Enter your email address..." 
								required 
								aria-label="Email address"
							/>
							<button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Follow My Journey</button>
						</form>
						<span class="privacy-note">🔒 No spam. Just honest&nbsp;notes.</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Recent Insights -->
			<section class="section-header" style="justify-content: center; text-align: center; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; margin: 5rem auto 2.5rem;">
				<h2 style="font-size: 2.75rem; font-weight: 800; color: #000000; letter-spacing: -1px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Recent Posts</h2>
				<p style="max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; color: #000000; font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.6; text-align: center; text-wrap: balance;">Here is what I've written about, the experiments I've conducted, and what I've discovered along the&nbsp;way.</p>
			</section>

			<div class="grid">
				{
					posts.slice(0, 3).map((post, index) => {
						// Entry #1 is the newest post on Monday
						const postNumber = index + 1;
						const category = post.data.category || (post.data.title.toLowerCase().includes('research') || post.data.title.toLowerCase().includes('carnivore') ? 'Research' : 'My Experience');
						return (
						<article class="card">
							<a href={`/blog/${post.id}/`}>
								<div class="card-img" style={`background-image: url(${typeof post.data.heroImage === 'string' ? post.data.heroImage : post.data.heroImage.src})`}></div>
								<div class="card-body">
									<div class="card-meta">
										<span class="meta-tag">{category}</span>
										<span class="meta-date">Entry #{postNumber} • <FormattedDate date={post.data.pubDate} /></span>
									</div>
									<h3>{post.data.title}</h3>
									<p>{post.data.description}</p>
									<span class="view-story">Read More →</span>
								</div>
							</a>
						</article>
					)})
				}
			</div>

			<div style="text-align: center; margin: 4rem 0;">
				<a href="/blog" class="btn btn-outline" style="padding: 0.85rem 2.25rem;">View All Entries +</a>
			</div>

			<!-- Newsletter Callout -->
			<section class="newsletter-section">
				<h2>You Don't Need To Navigate BMS&nbsp;Alone</h2>
				<p>Let's use the collective wisdom to solve BMS for more&nbsp;people.</p>
				<a href="/join" class="btn btn-primary" style="padding: 1rem 2.75rem; font-size: 1.05rem;">Participate With&nbsp;Me →</a>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
